      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Let \\( f(x) = 2x^3 - 4x^2 + 3x - 1 \\) and \\( g(x) = x^3 + 5x^2 - 2x + 4 \\). Find \\( f(x) + g(x) \\). Write your answer in standard form.",
      "inputs": [
        { "id": "s1q1_ans", "type": "text", "label": "Answer =", "answer": "3x^3 + x^2 + x + 3", "normalize": "poly" }
      ],
      "hint": "Add like terms for each degree: x^3, x^2, x, and constants separately.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (2+1)x^3 + (-4+5)x^2 + (3-2)x + (-1+4) = 3x^3 + x^2 + x + 3 \\)"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1q2",
