      "standard": "S1.a",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "type": "simplify",
      "question_html": "Let \\( f(x) = 3x^3 + 2x^2 - 5x + 1 \\) and \\( g(x) = x^3 - 4x^2 + 3x - 6 \\). Find \\( f(x) - g(x) \\). Write your answer in standard form.",
      "inputs": [
        { "id": "s1q2_ans", "type": "text", "label": "Answer =", "answer": "2x^3 + 6x^2 - 8x + 7", "normalize": "poly" }
      ],
      "hint": "Distribute the negative to every term of g(x) first, then combine like terms.",
      "solution_html": "\\( (3-1)x^3 + (2+4)x^2 + (-5-3)x + (1+6) = 2x^3 + 6x^2 - 8x + 7 \\)"
    },
